# TNG RESKIN - the conversion half of this mod, and it is OPT-IN.
#
# WHAT IT DOES. It declares the GAME'S OWN ship keys - `tsn_light_cruiser`,
# `kralien_battleship`, `starbase_command` - carrying TNG ships. An add-on entry overrides
# a key `data/shipData.yaml` already owns (engine-verified 1.3.5, missions/shipdata_override),
# so with this loaded every hull an old mission spawns is a Trek hull, and the mission does
# not know anything happened.
#
# WHY IT HAS TO EXIST SEPARATELY. The mod proper gives its ships their own `tng_*` keys,
# which is what makes it additive - a mission can spawn a Saber and a Light Cruiser in the
# same game, and two Trek mods can coexist. Nothing here changes that. But a mission written
# before this mod names STOCK keys, in literals, in its own content: LegendaryMissions
# hardcodes `enemyTypeNameList = ["Kralien", "Torgoth", "Arvonian"]` in every map and
# thirteen `station_type` keys across its maps and prefabs. None of it reads a setting, so
# no profile can point it at TNG art. This can, without editing a line of LM.
#
# LOADING IT IS A CHOICE, and an exclusive one. With this on, nothing can spawn a Light
# Cruiser as a Light Cruiser any more - the key IS a Saber now. That is what a conversion
# means, and it is why this is a separate add-on a profile opts into rather than something
# `tng_races` does to every mission that loads it.
#
#   LegendaryMissions/profiles/tng_total.yaml
#   python -m cosmos_dev.mission_runner . --map 0 --profile tng_total
#
# IT DOES NOT NEED `tng_races`. The hulls it declares are complete in themselves and the art
# is in the shared media pack, so a profile that wants the conversion and nothing else can
# include this alone. Loading both is fine and is what the profile does - you get the stock
# keys converted AND the `tng_*` keys available to anything that asks for them by name.
#
# `media/tng_reskin.json` is GENERATED by `_tools/make_reskin.py` from the stock->TNG map in
# `_build_from_zip.py`, so the mapping is written down once. It copies everything from the
# TNG entry except `key`, `side` and `roles`, which stay stock - those are not stats, they
# are how a mission FINDS a ship (`filter_ship_data_by_side`) and how docking and comms know
# a station is a station.
#
# THREE ENEMY STARBASES DO NOT CHANGE APPEARANCE: starbase_kralien, starbase_skaraan and
# starbase_torgoth map to TNG entries that themselves borrow stock art, because the pack
# ships no mesh for them. They convert their stats and keep their old hull. That is a gap in
# the art, not in this file.
tng_reskin_declared = ship_data_add_extra("tng_reskin", mod="tng_reskin")

# print, NOT log. log() is Python logging with no handler attached and is invisible in the
# engine, and this line is the only report of whether a CONVERSION took - the difference
# between a Trek game and a stock one, which is worth being able to see.
print("tng_reskin: stock hulls converted to TNG, engine=" + str(tng_reskin_declared))
